---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/site-config';
import { href } from '../lib/campaigns';
import { STATUS_LABELS, STATUSES } from '../lib/campaign-validation';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who runs this prototype, how it's maintained, and how to report inaccuracies.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About this project</h1>
    <p class="notice notice-warn">
      <strong>{siteConfig.disclaimer}.</strong> SFBA has not approved this site, its campaign wording or its
      public-comment suggestions, and doesn't operate it. No swimming, paddling or community group is a partner
      unless it's named here with its permission (none are yet).
    </p>

    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      An independently built demonstration of a coalition action center for San Francisco Bay shoreline access,
      offered to the San Francisco Boardsailing Association for review. It turns findings from SFBA's 2026
      report into specific actions anyone who uses the Bay can take: swimmers, paddlers, rowers, sailors, board
      sports, anglers and beach visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>What campaign statuses mean</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      {
        STATUSES.map((s) => (
          <>
            <dt>{STATUS_LABELS[s].short}</dt>
            <dd>{STATUS_LABELS[s].long}</dd>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <p>
      A campaign is only marked open for comment after its decision-maker, submission route and any deadline
      have been checked against an official source, and the date of that check is shown on the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Using AI to draft a comment</h2>
    <p>
      The comment helper doesn't call any AI service itself. It builds a prompt from the campaign and your
      optional answers. You choose whether to paste it into ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini, using your own free or paid
      account. The prompt tells the chatbot not to invent experiences, credentials or facts, and to ask you
      questions first if you haven't shared enough. You review and send the comment yourself. You can always
      write without AI using the talking points on each page.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts, analytics, tracking pixels or cookies.</li>
      <li>What you type into the helper stays in your browser tab. It isn't saved or sent to this site or to SFBA.</li>
      <li>If you choose to paste it into ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini, that company's privacy policy applies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections and maintenance</h2>
    <p>
      Campaigns are plain text files in the <a href={siteConfig.repoUrl}>project repository</a>, so anyone can
      see what changed and when. To report an inaccuracy, an outdated date or contact, or evidence about how a
      decision affects your activity, <a href={siteConfig.correctionsUrl}>open an issue</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>If SFBA adopts it</h2>
    <p>
      The project is built to be handed over: the repository can be transferred to an SFBA-controlled account,
      linked from sfba.org or served from a custom subdomain. Editorial ownership, the disclaimer and these
      pages would then be updated to reflect SFBA's decisions.
    </p>
    <p><a href={href()}>← Back to campaigns</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
